Sam says the interior angle of this sector is $250^{\circ}$ because that is the angle marked. Explain the mistake and find the interior angle.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw (O) -- (0:2.4) arc[start angle=0,end angle=110,radius=2.4] -- cycle;
\draw (110:0.7) arc[start angle=110,end angle=360,radius=0.7];
\path (235:1.15) node {$250^{\circ}$};
\fill (O) circle (1.6pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The marked angle sweeps outside the sector, so $250^{\circ}$ is the exterior angle.

$\begin{aligned}\text{interior} &=360^{\circ}-250^{\circ}\\&=110^{\circ}\end{aligned}$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw (O) -- (0:2.4) arc[start angle=0,end angle=110,radius=2.4] -- cycle;
\draw (110:0.7) arc[start angle=110,end angle=360,radius=0.7];
\path (235:1.15) node {$250^{\circ}$};
\draw (0:0.85) arc[start angle=0,end angle=110,radius=0.85];
\path (55:1.35) node {$110^{\circ}$};
\fill (O) circle (1.6pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
